From 702dbf02a45ae8722409456c846cef0aa4cdb0d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 13:33:53 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(2d): rest machining on the 2D Pocket from the
 previous operations

The rest group of the 2D Pocket gets a mode. "Entered tool" is the
behaviour of #1489. "Previous operations" reads the stock that the earlier
operations of the setup leave (rest::prior_state), at every cut depth of
the Pocket.

- motion: RestSource on RestParams; rest_pocket_previous,
  rest_plan_stock and rest_stock_from_columns (rest_prior.rs) build a
  RestStock from the column grid. A column stands when its top is above a
  cut depth. Standing columns grow by one cell diagonal. A column that
  cannot be read, and the pocket outside the grid, stand. The rest area is
  the union over all cut depths.
- The two modes never use each other's planner: each refuses by name.
- app: the Pocket arm routes the mode; job collection refuses by name a
  tilted plane and an earlier operation that has no toolpath, a stale
  toolpath, or is suppressed with a cut on record. The project key
  rest.source and the MCP parameter ride the existing DTO. The stamp gets
  the byte 0xD8 in the new mode only.
- ui: the "Rest stock from" row; the previous tool rows hide in the new
  mode.

Invalidation uses the program-ahead digest that each unposed operation
already has in its stamp.

Fixes #2033

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
